// munch_priority.anka: maximal munch (longest match wins) and
// rule priority (on a tie in length, the rule listed first wins).
// C4   keyword vs identifier: if -> IF (tie, priority); ifx iffy if_ _if -> IDENT (munch)
// C5   keywords are case-sensitive: If WHILE True Print -> IDENT
// C6   all 16 keywords, each one token
// C7   every one-char / two-char operator pair, plus % and ..
// C8   && and || are tokens; a single & or | is an error
// C9   a-->b  -> IDENT MINUS ARROW IDENT
// C10  x**-2  -> IDENT POW MINUS INT_LIT;  x**=2 -> IDENT POW ASSIGN INT_LIT (no **= operator)
// C11  no spaces at all: munch still splits correctly
// C12  all 7 punctuation marks

if ifx iffy if_ _if
If WHILE True Print
fn let if else while for in return break continue print int float bool true false
= == ! != < <= > >= + += - -= -> * *= ** / /= % ..
a && b || c & d | e
a-->b
x**-2 x**=2
x=y==z<=w&&!v
( ) { } ; , :
